y gripes it'd probably be  with the way sombras reveal was handled  now I like alternate reality games just  as much as the next person but blizzards  decision to draw the reveal all four  months going from one fake website to  another with timer after timer counting  down to nothing with no end in sight it  just kind of tired everyone out after a  while it just wasn't fun anymore and  people just bleeding for it to end so  far over watches new heroes and maps it  gets a B+ for me and I just hope  Blizzard can keep the future releases  just as hype one thing they I'm sure a  lot of us were hoping for this past year  was a single-player mode of sorts  anything that would further detail  overwatch a story line but Blizzard seem  to be content on doing their own thing  and delivering the characters  backstories very very gradually through  short films comics and blog posts I  think this is probably the smarter way  to go about things as it keeps players  interested and lets each new story  update soak in the game does have a lot  to work with but I would personally love  to see more plot based seasonal events  you know stuff like the uprising event  that is canned into the overwatch  universe but until then  overwatch gets a B+ in the story  Department there's little doubt that  Blizzard has been hitting it way out of  the park with their seasonal events the  summer games Halloween terror winter  wonderland year the rooster and uprising  have each displayed blizzards strengths  in creating exciting events each one has  given players new skins emote swing  poses sprays as well as fun arcade modes  that showcase just how well the game can  morph into different styles okay maybe I  could have done without the turtle fest  that was capture the flag but joking  sans revenge was pretty spectacular and  the holiday-themed masks were a joy to  play  Jamison Junkins time overall it's an  a-minus balancing is tough work just ask  this guy right here within the first few  months 